# Pairs with OwnerMonotonic. The registry retires the saga's row as soon as the
# saga has decided rather than once its terminal fan-out has completed, so a
# bucket the fan-out has not yet resolved is read against an absent row - as
# InFlight - and a committed key reads its pre-saga value again.
MODULE: OwnerMonotonicForgetBeforeFanOut
TARGET: OwnerMonotonic
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the registry forgets a decided saga before its terminals land, so a committed key reverts
PERTURBS: RegistryForget

--- FIND
RegistryForget ==
    /\ sg = "done"
--- REPLACE
RegistryForget ==
\* MUTATION: the row is retired once the saga decides, not once it completes.
    /\ sg \in {"decided", "done"}
--- END
